WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.527
Views solve several problems at once.

00:00:02.527 --> 00:00:05.812
They let us centralize shared SQL logic.

00:00:05.812 --> 00:00:10.157
They create a stable interface with deliberate columns and row meaning.

00:00:10.157 --> 00:00:14.692
They can reduce accidental exposure by omitting unnecessary fields,

00:00:14.692 --> 00:00:19.352
although actual authorization still depends on database security controls.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:24.882
And materialized views can store reusable results when freshness does not need to be immediate.

00:00:24.882 --> 00:00:29.882
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:29.882 --> 00:00:36.287
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:36.287 --> 00:00:42.560
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
